20:13:57 said  I built a terminal app in your workspace that brings together the server-and-costs view with the settings and operations tools from the extra folder you added. You can browse servers and containers with live-looking usage and cost details, add or remove a server with on-screen forms, and manage each product’s settings with checks, clearer warnings, secret hiding/reveal, and secret generation; the extra folder has been removed after its useful parts were folded in.
20:13:57 said  It follows the overall layout and controls you asked for, but some parts are still simulated for safety here: live server/container data and stack actions (start, stop, migrate, logs) show realistic behavior and example commands rather than running real remote or Docker changes. A few technical quality warnings also remain in the new behind-the-scenes helpers.
20:13:57 said  What’s still uncertain is how this will behave against your real servers, tunnels, and compose environments without a live connection and real data. A good next step is to try it with one real product or server setup and tell me which actions or checks you want it to perform for real first.
